{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat /Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/d375-measure/packet-v5-1.md'","aggregated_output":"# Packet v5-1\n\n**The question:** How much will Nvidia's total revenue grow in FY2028?\n\nDue 2028-02-29. Possible answers:\n- 1 Strongly bullish: FY2028 total revenue growth is at least 80%.\n- 2 Bullish: FY2028 total revenue growth is at least 70% and below 80%.\n- 3 Neutral: FY2028 total revenue growth is at least 45% and below 70%.\n- 4 Bearish: FY2028 total revenue growth is at least 25% and below 45%.\n- 5 Strongly bearish: FY2028 total revenue growth is below 25%.\n\n**16 statements read on 2026-09-22:**\n\n- **v5-1-1** (stored attribution: AI Singapore): AI Singapore is adding Nvidia Nemotron open models and NeMo tools to its SEA-LION model family.\n  - Passage: \"This includes AI Singapore adding Nemotron open models and NeMo tools to SEA-LION, its model family for Southeast Asian languages and cultures.\"\n- **v5-1-2** (stored attribution: iApp Technology): Thailand's iApp Technology is adapting Nvidia Nemotron 3 Nano for Thai-language legal work.\n  - Passage: \"Meanwhile, Thailand's iApp Technology is adapting Nemotron 3 Nano for Thai-language legal work.\"\n- **v5-1-3** (stored attribution: TweakTown): TweakTown reported that US third-party RTX 5070 card prices had risen from around $650 a couple of months earlier to around $850, attributing the increase to the RAM crisis.\n  - Passage: \"I expect the RTX 5070 PCs will last longer - they're both still in stock at the time of writing - but even these represent a decent bargain given that you're looking at around $850 for a third-party card in the US these days. That's up from around $650 just a couple of months ago, and GPU pricing is getting a whole lot worse thanks to the RAM crisis.\"\n- **v5-1-4** (stored attribution: NVIDIA): NVIDIA said Remedy Entertainment’s CONTROL Resonant is scheduled to launch on September 24, 2026, with DLSS 4.5 and path tracing.\n  - Passage: \"Remedy Entertainment’s CONTROL Resonant is launching September 24th with DLSS 4.5 and path tracing.\"\n- **v5-1-5** (stored attribution: Sea): Sea plans to adopt Nvidia's Vera Rubin platform across Shopee, Monee and Garena to build and deploy AI models and agents at greater scale.\n  - Passage: \"Singapore-founded Sea will adopt Nvidia's Vera Rubin platform to build and deploy artificial-intelligence (AI) models and agents at greater scale across its Shopee, Monee and Garena businesses.\"\n- **v5-1-6** (stored attribution: NCS): NCS adopted Nvidia Nemotron models and a video-search-and-summarisation blueprint for enterprise and public-sector work.\n  - Passage: \"For instance, NCS has adopted Nemotron models and its video-search-and-summarisation blueprint for enterprise and public-sector work.\"\n- **v5-1-7** (stored attribution: videocardz.com): Videocardz.com reported that a CyberPowerPC system with an RTX 5080 Founders Edition, priced at $2,299, sold out in one day after receiving more than 1,000 orders; the period was one day, with no specific date given.\n  - Passage: \"I think the $2,299 system that sold out in one day with over 1,000 orders makes sense given how much RTX 5080 cards cost now.\"\n- **v5-1-8** (stored attribution: NCS): NCS is developing physical-AI applications for humanoid robotics.\n  - Passage: \"NCS is also developing physical-AI applications for humanoid robotics.\"\n- **v5-1-9** (stored attribution: CyberPowerPC): CyberPowerPC began shipping prebuilt gaming PCs with NVIDIA GeForce RTX 50 Founders Edition GPUs for sale through Walmart during its September 21–27, 2026 GeForce Week promotion.\n  - Passage: \"CyberPowerPC is now shipping prebuilt gaming PCs with NVIDIA’s own GeForce RTX 50 Founders Edition graphics cards. The systems are being sold through Walmart as part of the retailer’s GeForce Week promotion, which runs from September 21 through September 27.\"\n- **v5-1-10** (stored attribution: Singapore's Home Team Science and Technology Agency (HTX)): Singapore's HTX is beginning research using two Nvidia Nemotron models for public-safety applications.\n  - Passage: \"Meanwhile, Singapore's Home Team Science and Technology Agency (HTX) is beginning research using two Nemotron models for public-safety applications.\"\n- **v5-1-11** (stored attribution: NVIDIA): NVIDIA said AION 2’s global release on September 30, 2026, will include DLSS 4.5 Super Resolution and Multi Frame Generation support for GeForce RTX GPUs.\n  - Passage: \"When the global version is released on September 30th, AION 2 will include support for DLSS 4.5 Super Resolution and Multi Frame Generation, enabling the highest levels of image quality and performance on all GeForce RTX GPUs.\"\n- **v5-1-12** (stored attribution: Viettel AI): Viettel AI fine-tuned Nvidia Nemotron 3 Super for Vietnamese-language and agentic applications, and plans to use it in Legal AI for Viettel employees and external customers.\n  - Passage: \"In Vietnam, Viettel AI has fine-tuned Nemotron 3 Super for Vietnamese-language and agentic applications. The model is set to be used in Legal AI, an agent system for Viettel Group employees and external customers.\"\n- **v5-1-13** (stored attribution: VideoCardz): VideoCardz reported that Walmart sold more than 1,000 CyberPowerPC systems with RTX 5080 GPUs in one day before they sold out.\n  - Passage: \"According to VideoCardz, the cheaper RTX 5080 systems sold out in a day flat, with Walmart shifting over 1,000 units apparently.\"\n- **v5-1-14** (stored attribution: NVIDIA): NVIDIA said it will deliver additional NVIDIA features in The Witcher 3: Wild Hunt — Remastered on September 29, 2026.\n  - Passage: \"And on September 29th, NVIDIA will be delivering even more cutting-edge features through Remastered.\"\n- **v5-1-15** (stored attribution: ST Engineering): ST Engineering is using Nvidia NeMo tools and cuOpt software to develop its AI Studio platform and deploy applications, including for marine maintenance, repair and overhaul.\n  - Passage: \"At ST Engineering, Nvidia's NeMo tools and cuOpt software are being used to develop its AI Studio platform and deploy AI applications in areas including marine maintenance, repair and overhaul.\"\n- **v5-1-16** (stored attribution: NVIDIA): NVIDIA said its technical partnership with The Coalition enables GeForce RTX features—including DLSS Super Resolution, Dynamic Multi Frame Generation, Reflex and ray tracing—in Gears of War: E-Day.\n  - Passage: \"Thanks to a technical partnership with Gears of War: E-Day developer The Coalition, GeForce RTX gamers can activate a suite of features to accelerate and further enhance Gears of War: E-Day, delivering the definitive PC experience:\nDLSS Super Resolution and Dynamic Multi Frame Generation will multiply frame rates, whilst simultaneously increasing image quality.\nNVIDIA Reflex will reduce PC latency, making gameplay even more responsive, and possibly giving you a competitive edge in Versus.\nAnd the Ray Tracing cores found in all GeForce RTX GPUs will accelerate the rendering of Unreal Engine 5.8’s Lumen and MegaLights ray tracing technologies.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"item\":\"v5-1-1\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"Model adoption does not give an estimate of Nvidia's FY2028 revenue growth.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v5-1-2\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"Adapting a model does not indicate Nvidia's FY2028 revenue growth.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v5-1-3\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"Third-party card prices do not establish Nvidia's revenue or its FY2028 growth.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v5-1-4\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"A game launch with Nvidia features does not indicate FY2028 total revenue growth.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v5-1-5\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The adoption plan gives no spending amount or timing that would indicate FY2028 revenue growth.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v5-1-6\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"Model and tool adoption does not indicate Nvidia's FY2028 revenue growth.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v5-1-7\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"One day's sales of a particular PC do not indicate Nvidia's FY2028 total revenue growth.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v5-1-8\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"NCS's robotics work gives no indication of Nvidia's FY2028 revenue growth.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v5-1-9\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"A 2026 PC promotion does not indicate Nvidia's FY2028 total revenue growth.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v5-1-10\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"Research using two models does not indicate Nvidia's FY2028 revenue growth.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v5-1-11\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"A game release with Nvidia features does not indicate FY2028 total revenue growth.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v5-1-12\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The planned use of a model does not indicate Nvidia's FY2028 revenue growth.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v5-1-13\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"One day's sales of a particular PC do not indicate Nvidia's FY2028 total revenue growth.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v5-1-14\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"A 2026 game feature update does not indicate Nvidia's FY2028 revenue growth.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v5-1-15\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"Use of Nvidia's tools gives no revenue amount or timing for FY2028.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v5-1-16\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"A game partnership does not indicate Nvidia's FY2028 total revenue growth.\"}\n{\"done\":true,\"items\":16}"}}
